@startuml 4_2_Lobby_StateMachine
' MyBattleship -- GroupXXAssign2.pdf, section 4.2: Lobby (state diagram)
' Models the Lobby class lifecycle (LobbyStatus enum from the analysis class list).
title MyBattleship -- Lobby Lifecycle (State Machine)

hide empty description
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 75
skinparam padding 5
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam StateFontSize 14
skinparam StateAttributeFontSize 12
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
  ArrowColor Black
}

[*] --> Waiting : createLobby(name, gameType)\n[name length 1..16 or blank]\n/ generateCode(), seat host

state Waiting : entry / shareLink() shown to host
state Waiting : do / await second player
state Waiting : keepLobbyOpen() / lastSeenAt = now (host's page, every 10 s)

state InProgress : entry / Game created in PLACEMENT
state InProgress : do / run match (see section 4.1 (Game))

state Finished : entry / results built from shot history
state Abandoned : entry / code stops resolving

Waiting --> Waiting : joinLobby(code)\n[isFull() or not isJoinable()]\n/ return JoinError
Waiting --> InProgress : joinLobby(code)\n[isJoinable() and not isFull()]\n/ seat guest, notify both clients
Waiting --> Abandoned : joinLobby(code) or sweep\n[isHostGone(): no check-in > 30 s, no guest seated]\n/ abandon()

InProgress --> Finished : gameEnded(endReason)\n[winner declared]\n/ status = FINISHED
InProgress --> [*] : sweep\n[idle > 24 h]\n/ row deleted

Finished --> InProgress : requestRematch(code, true)\n[isMutual()]\n/ reset(), same code reused
Finished --> Abandoned : requestRematch(code, false)\n[declined, or a player left with Home]\n/ status = ABANDONED
Finished --> [*] : sweep\n[no answer, idle > 24 h]\n/ row deleted

Abandoned --> [*] : sweep\n[abandoned > 1 h]\n/ row deleted

note right of Waiting
  Guard source: requirement 1.1
  "delete a waiting lobby if the host is
  disconnected for 30 seconds before a
  guest joins". The server can't see presence,
  so the host's page checks in instead.
  The pg_cron sweep runs every 15 minutes.
end note
@enduml
